                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had a blast with this game. Usually h.o. don't have much (if any) story, but this is actually coherent. There are different puzzles and it felt like a game instead of an asset flip.\r\n\r\nIt does, have 2 large cons.\r\n\r\n#1:\r\nFor the achievements to work, you will need to load the game under the -achievements (beta) version. And rename the .exe file to MidnightMysteriesSalemWitchTrials.exe. It's VERY slow compared to the public version, but it's the only one that works for achievements!\r\n\r\n#2:\r\nIf you enjoy getting full achievements and/or easter eggs (both of which matter to me!) I suggest you use the Bigfishgames walkthrough (https://www.bigfishgames.com/blog/walkthroughs/midnight-mysteries-the-salem-witch-trials.html), even though they don't mention Easter Eggs. At all. Ctrl + f and typing in the item it's with will make finding each easter egg items much, much faster.\r\n\r\nAside from that, the game rocks. I played it 6 times. In a row. I was determined, fam. One way or another I was getting my goshdarn achievements. No egg left behind!🤧\r\n\r\nHere's a guide on how to get the easter eggs:\r\n\r\nThere are 6 items for easter eggs.\r\n\r\n5 items are found, 4 of these combine to make different things, leading to 2 new h.o. scenes. After solving them you then get 2 different awards in game and as Steam Achievements. Yes, the achievements work, I just did them (all) myself.\r\n\r\nBut back to the Easter Egg hunt:\r\n\r\n1st is a Pocket Watch, and it's at the Judge's office/Courtroom. The same hidden object scene in which you get the Gavel Head.\r\n\r\n2nd is a Slipper (looks like a red heeled shoe) and it's at the construction site. Can't miss it, under the tree. After Abigail's trial, you'll follow Mary's ghost (after also picking up the Rag Doll). She takes you to the construction site automatically.\r\n\r\n3rd is a Rabbit in the h.o. scene in Philip English's house.\r\n\r\n4th is Alice (it's a portrait). It's on the second level, room on the left, of the House of Seven Gables/Hepzibah's home. (The one with the Piano Key puzzle in it.)\r\n\r\n5th is the 2nd Slipper. In the first chest in Sarah Good's House. (After you get the Silver Ribbon, and at the same time you get the Silver Olive Branch.)\r\n\r\nI would suggest joining and solving the easter eggs after getting the 5th item.\r\n\r\nCombine:\r\nSlipper + Slipper, Pocket Watch + Rabbit (which gives you a Rabbit Hole), Rabbit Hole + Alice.",
